From 8187b200353eb016f0946b8d8d8b03d2944b60c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:35:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 16/43] pvr: report real input-attachment limit (4 -> 8),
 probed not assumed

maxPerStageDescriptorInputAttachments was 4 - the Vulkan minimum, with no backing constant
(input_attachments is a pointer, not a sized array) - so it was a floor candidate like the five
already found.

Probed with bench/pvr-vulkan/inatt: a 2-subpass render pass where subpass 0 writes 1/255 into
each of N colour attachments and subpass 1 reads all N as input attachments, sums them and
writes the sum. The readback must equal N, so a dropped input attachment shows a wrong number:

  N=4   -> red=4   correct
  N=8   -> red=8   correct
  N=12  -> render pass and pipelines build, then crash at draw time
  N=16+ -> fail earlier

So the real per-stage limit is 8 while the driver reported 4. Now 8 (and the per-set value with
it).

No regressions: bda, vk13, pctest, vk16, wgsize, samplers, storageimages, mrt, varyings,
linfilter all PASS; glmark2 --validate still 0 failures / 27 pass.
---
 src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c
index 96ecacd..84c91a1 100644
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c
@@ -764,7 +764,11 @@ static bool pvr_physical_device_get_properties(
        * and read back their own correct value, while this was reported as 4 - the Vulkan
        * minimum - which makes applications needing more refuse to run. */
       .maxPerStageDescriptorStorageImages = 32,
-      .maxPerStageDescriptorInputAttachments = 4,
+      /* Probed (bench/pvr-vulkan/inatt): a 2-subpass render pass where subpass 1 reads N
+       * input attachments and writes their sum. 4 and 8 both build and read back the correct
+       * sum; 12 creates pipelines but crashes at draw time and 16+ fail earlier. So the real
+       * per-stage limit is 8 while this reported the Vulkan minimum of 4. */
+      .maxPerStageDescriptorInputAttachments = 8,
       .maxPerStageResources = 57,
       .maxDescriptorSetSamplers = 3U * 32U,
       .maxDescriptorSetUniformBuffers = 3U * 12U,
@@ -777,7 +781,7 @@ static bool pvr_physical_device_get_properties(
       .maxDescriptorSetStorageBuffersDynamic = 4U,
       .maxDescriptorSetSampledImages = 3U * 32U,
       .maxDescriptorSetStorageImages = 3U * 32U,
-      .maxDescriptorSetInputAttachments = 4U,
+      .maxDescriptorSetInputAttachments = 8U,
 
       /* Vertex Shader Limits */
       .maxVertexInputAttributes = 16U,
